INT. LUMENFLOW - OPEN-PLAN OFFICE - DAY

Standing desks. Bean bags. A neon sign: MOVE FAST. A WAITER in a vest sets out catered sandwiches. Two TEENAGERS on a school tour peer at a whiteboard. A DOG sleeps under a desk.

TAVI BROOKS, 30s, they/them, hoodie, stares at a laptop. Across the row, RHEA NAKAGAWA, 40s, CEO, reads a printed memo upside down, as if that's how it came.

OSEI, 20s, engineer, carries three monitors and sets none of them down.

RHEA
Tavi. Got a sec?

TAVI
Not really.

Rhea waits. Tavi's cursor blinks.

TAVI (CONT'D)
Okay.

They walk to the glass room. The waiter's tray clinks behind them.

INT. GLASS CONFERENCE ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Rhea closes the door. Doesn't sit.

RHEA
Series B didn't close.

TAVI
I saw the Slack.

RHEA
Payroll's Friday.

Tavi's thumb rubs the edge of the table.

TAVI
They told me they'd cover through spring.

RHEA
Who did?

TAVI
You did.

Outside, Osei finally sets a monitor down. Picks it up again.

The intercom CRACKLES.

RECEPTIONIST (V.O.)
Rhea, there's a gentleman here from the board.

RHEA
(into the room)
Tell him five minutes.

RECEPTIONIST (V.O.)
He says he's already on his way up.

Tavi's phone lights up on the table.

ON PHONE (TEXT): osei: tell me u didn't sign it

Tavi turns it face-down. Rhea sees.

RHEA
Did you?

TAVI
I put my name where it was asked for.

Through the glass, the dog stands, stretches, trots toward the elevator.

The elevator DINGS.
